@startuml activity-find-collect
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because this is a control flow with several filter branches AND swimlane ownership
'' that is the point of the design — everything in the second lane is DOM-free and unit-tested, everything
'' in the first and third touches the DOM. Mermaid cannot express coloured lanes plus a banner-free,
'' byte-reproducible SVG. Palette: green #67B11D DOM work, blue-violet #7590DB the pure core,
'' amber/red for the rejected paths.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title How a match is collected — from the content pane to a painted Range

|#DCEBD4|DOM shell (renderer.find)|
start
:query normalized;
if (blank query?) then (yes)
  :clear! — delete both highlights,\ndisconnect the observer; <<ERROR_TINT>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
:TreeWalker over .vv-content\n(SHOW_ELEMENT | SHOW_TEXT); <<MARKDOWN_FILL>>

repeat :next node;
  if (text node?) then (yes)
    :emit {:kind :text :id i :s data}; <<MARKDOWN_TINT>>
    if (nearest HARD ancestor changed?) then (yes)
      :emit {:kind :hard}  → "\n" in the buffer; <<MARKDOWN_TINT>>
    else (no)
      if (parent is inline-block?) then (yes)
        :emit {:kind :soft}  → " " in the buffer; <<MARKDOWN_TINT>>
      else (no)
      endif
    endif
  else (element)
    if (script/style/template/form control?\nSVG title/desc/metadata/defs?\n[hidden] or aria-hidden?\n**<mjx-assistive-mml>**?) then (reject)
      :FILTER_REJECT — prune the whole subtree; <<ERROR_TINT>>
    else (keep)
      :one memoized getComputedStyle\nkeyed by parentTag|parentClass|tag|class; <<MAIN_TINT>>
      if (display:none or visibility:hidden?) then (yes)
        :FILTER_REJECT; <<ERROR_TINT>>
      else (no)
        if (<br>?) then (yes)
          :emit {:kind :soft}; <<MARKDOWN_TINT>>
        else (no)
          :FILTER_SKIP — descend, yield nothing; <<MAIN_FILL>>
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif
repeat while (more nodes?) is (yes) not (no)

|#DDE1F0|pure core (renderer.find-scan) — no DOM, unit-tested|
:**build** — fold the token stream into\nB (lower-cased, whitespace-collapsed)\n+ segment quads [b n o len]; <<APPDB_FILL>>
note right
  SAFE-LOWER is length-preserving:
  "İ".toLowerCase() is TWO UTF-16 units,
  which would desynchronise every index
  after it from its node offset.
end note
:**scan** — non-overlapping indexOf over B; <<APPDB_TINT>>
note right
  normalize-query TRIMS, so a match can
  never begin or end on a separator — and
  can never contain "\n". A match may span
  a :soft boundary, never a :hard one.
end note
:**locate** — binary-search the quads at\n<latex>s</latex> and <latex>e-1</latex>, inverting <latex>\lambda</latex>; <<APPDB_TINT>>

|#DCEBD4|DOM shell (renderer.find)|
if (both endpoints resolved?) then (no)
  :drop this match; <<ERROR_TINT>>
else (yes)
  :Range.setStart / setEnd —\n**may span nodes**; <<MARKDOWN_FILL>>
endif
:Highlight.add <latex>\forall</latex> matches\nCSS.highlights.set "vv-find" / "vv-find-current"; <<MARKDOWN_FILL>>
:**confined** scrollTo the focused Range's rect\n(never el.scrollIntoView); <<MARKDOWN_TINT>>
:re-measure on the next frame and correct —\na content-visibility block only gets a real\nheight once it is scrolled into view; <<MAIN_TINT>>
stop

legend right
  |= Colour |= Lane / concept |
  |<#DCEBD4>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| DOM shell — walk, Ranges, painting, scrolling |
  |<#DDE1F0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| pure core — flatten, scan, locate (DOM-free, unit-tested) |
  |<#67B11D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| a step that produces a token, a Range, or a highlight |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| style resolution / geometry (the memoized, costly part) |
  |<#E0211D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| rejected — not searchable text |
endlegend
@enduml
